Healthcare guidance for the worlds:
- Set the worlds in everyday Indian places where these patients and their families live, work, study, play, celebrate or travel — homes, neighbourhoods, workplaces, schools, playgrounds, festivals, commutes.
- At most one world may be set in or around the hospital or clinic, and it must feel calm and human (a reception area, a waiting lounge, a hospital garden) — never an operation theatre, ICU or emergency scene.
- If the patients include children (ages 0–7 or 8–15), include at least one family or child-centred setting.
- No world should show illness, injury, pain or distress.

